# Code owners of the stage A demo stand. With the candidate/a ruleset's code-owner review, a PR
# that changes any path below cannot merge without an approval from @XThoughtLabs, the CEO's account.
# It covers every path the gate protects (gate.guard G-1, G-1a, G-1b, and quality.toml's
# [guard] lists), the acceptance tests, every conftest.py, the test, coverage and security
# configuration, and the dependencies (the customer's letter of 2026-11-13, section 4), and the
# paths the guard marks for a person in needs_code_owner under G-1b-mark, G-1c and G-8.
# Ordinary tests (tests/, test_*.py, *_test.py) are not listed since HQ-TASK-M1-B2, so that a
# queue PR adding ordinary tests can merge without a person. A deleted, skipped or weakened
# existing test still fails gate/guard (G-2 to G-4), a required check; any other change to an
# existing test (the guard's mark, G-4a) must get no automatic admission from the controller's
# required check stage-a/policy.
# GitHub matches these paths in their exact letter case; the guard matches any case.

